fragment_downloaded_cb({"url":"Reference-manual_builtin_meson.html#arguments10","fragment":"Arguments\nThe method meson.override_find_program() accepts the following positional arguments:\n\nFinally, meson.override_find_program()\naccepts the following keyword arguments:\n\n\n\n    \n      \n        Name\n        Type\n        Description\n        Tags\n      \n    \n    \n      \n        progname\n        str\n        \n        \nThe name of the program to override.\n  \n        \n\n  \n  \n      \n      \n        program\n        \nexe | file | program\n\n        \n        \nThe program to set as the override for progname.\n  \n        \n\n  \n  \n      \n    \n  \n\n    \n      \n        Name\n        Type\n        Description\n        Tags\n      \n    \n    \n      \n        native\n        bool\n        \n        \nIf set to true, the override produces output that can be used on the\nbuild machine, and will be returned by find_program(..., native : true),\notherwise (the default) the output is for the host machine. This\nis an important distinction when cross compiling.\n  \n        \n\n  (since 1.12.0)\n  default =\n  false\n  \n  \n      \n    \n  \n"});